'''Kingston Technology Corporation''' is an American multinational computer technology corporation that develops, manufactures, sells and supports [[computer]] memory products such as [[memory module]]s, [[solid-state drive]]s, and other [[flash memory]] products. It founded the HyperX gaming brand, but then sold it to [[HP Inc.|HP]].<ref>{{cite press release|title=HP Inc. to Acquire HyperX|url=https://press.hp.com/us/en/press-releases/2021/hp-inc-to-acquire-hyperx.html|access-date=2021-09-30|website=press.hp.com|language=en-US}}</ref> The company is headquartered in [[Fountain Valley, California]], United States and has manufacturing and logistics facilities in the United States, the [[United Kingdom]], [[Ireland]], [[Taiwan]], and [[China]].

It is the largest independent producer of [[Dynamic random access memory|DRAM]] memory modules.<ref name=":0" /> In 2018 the company generated $7.5 billion in revenue and made {{abbr|No.|Number}}{{sp}}53 on the ''[[Forbes]]'' list of "America's Largest Private Companies 2019", it made {{abbr|No.|Number}}{{sp}}28 on list of "America's Largest Private Companies 2025" .<ref>{{cite web|title=Kingston Technology Company|url=https://www.forbes.com/companies/kingston-technology-company/|access-date=2020-07-09|website=Forbes|language=en}}</ref> Kingston serves an international network of distributors, resellers, retailers and [[OEM]] customers on six continents. The company also provides [[contract manufacturing]] and [[supply chain]] management services for [[semiconductor]] manufacturers and system OEMs.

